  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\), \\(AB=AC\\), and \\(AD\\) bisects \\(\\angle BAC\\), meeting \\(BC\\) at \\(D\\). The criterion for proving \\(\\triangle ABD\\cong\\triangle ACD\\) is:",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "SAS",
    "B": "SSS",
    "C": "ASA",
    "D": "HL"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(AB=AC\\), \\(\\angle BAD=\\angle CAD\\) (angle bisector), and \\(AD=AD\\) (common side). Two sides and their included angle are respectively equal, so use SAS.",
